   <dc:description>ABSTRACT: Herein we report an atypical coloration in one individual of the yellow-striped poisonous frog,&#xd;
Dendrobates truncatus, in Colombian Magdalena middle valley. The adult individual presented&#xd;
leucism, a rare phenomenon occurs in nature or at very low frequencies.</dc:description>
